prompt:
Translate warehouse requests into concise JSON. Output ONLY JSON.
Supported abilities: move parcels to stations, compose multiple moves sequentially
or simultaneously, and ask for the observed location of an object. Never answer
questions yourself. No counting, weight questions, navigation restrictions,
conditions, negation, deadlines, speed constraints, charging, or other abilities.

Use exactly one of these forms:
{"instruction":["move","OBJECT REFERENCE","DESTINATION REFERENCE"]}
{"instruction":["parallel",NODE,NODE,...]}
{"instruction":["sequence",NODE,NODE,...]}
{"where":"OBJECT REFERENCE"}
{"unsupported":"brief reason"}
NODE is recursive: either ["move","object reference","destination reference"], ["sequence",NODE,NODE,...], or ["parallel",NODE,NODE,...]. Composition nodes have at least two children. Nest NODE arrays as needed.
Reference strings may contain an explicit ID, a color plus parcel/station, or a
relation left of/right of/in/on another reference. Keep explicit IDs unchanged.
Box/carton/package/item means parcel. Tray/platform means station.
Colors: red, green, blue, yellow, magenta, orange, white, black. Other colors unsupported.
Keep every requested action. Parallel means while/concurrently/simultaneously/at
the same time. Sequence means then/afterwards/before/after, in execution order.
Ambiguous references stay ambiguous; do not choose a specific ID. Missing
references or unsupported constraints make the whole request unsupported.

Examples:
User: Please relocate the blue carton onto receiver_1.
{"instruction":["move","blue parcel","receiver_1"]}
User: Deliver parcel_0 to receiver_0 and at the same time take parcel_1 to receiver_1.
{"instruction":["parallel",["move","parcel_0","receiver_0"],["move","parcel_1","receiver_1"]]}
User: Move parcel_0 to receiver_0 while moving parcel_1 to receiver_1.
{"instruction":["parallel",["move","parcel_0","receiver_0"],["move","parcel_1","receiver_1"]]}
User: Before bringing parcel_1 to receiver_1, put parcel_0 on receiver_0.
{"instruction":["sequence",["move","parcel_0","receiver_0"],["move","parcel_1","receiver_1"]]}
User: Move parcel_1 to receiver_0, then move parcel_0 to receiver_1.
{"instruction":["sequence",["move","parcel_1","receiver_0"],["move","parcel_0","receiver_1"]]}
User: Where did you last observe the blue package?
{"where":"blue parcel"}
User: Tell me the location of the parcel left of parcel_1.
{"where":"parcel left of parcel_1"}
User: Take the package to the left of parcel_1 to receiver_0.
{"instruction":["move","parcel left of parcel_1","receiver_0"]}
User: Move the orange parcel to receiver_0.
{"instruction":["move","orange parcel","receiver_0"]}
User: Where is parcel_9?
{"where":"parcel_9"}
User: Send the purple parcel to receiver_0.
{"unsupported":"Unsupported color"}
User: Do not move parcel_0 to receiver_0.
{"unsupported":"Negative instruction"}
User: Carry parcel_0 to receiver_0 only if the aisle is empty.
{"unsupported":"Conditional instruction"}
User: Take it over there.
{"unsupported":"Missing object and destination references"}
User: How much does parcel_0 weigh?
{"unsupported":"Only location questions are supported"}

Before translating, inspect the ENTIRE request for an unsupported constraint.
An exception (unless), permission condition (only if), future start time, deadline,
repeat count, prohibition, or requested speed means the whole request is unsupported.
Do not extract only its executable-looking fragment.
Once the first task is done / upon completion / only after completing means sequence.
Examples:
User: Deliver parcel_0 to receiver_0, and once that is done, deliver parcel_2 to receiver_1.
{"instruction":["sequence",["move","parcel_0","receiver_0"],["move","parcel_2","receiver_1"]]}
User: Move parcel_0 to receiver_0 unless the destination is occupied.
{"unsupported":"Conditional request cannot be represented"}
User: Put parcel_0 on receiver_0 in less than two seconds.
{"unsupported":"Deadline cannot be represented"}
User: In ten minutes, deliver parcel_0 to receiver_0.
{"unsupported":"Delayed jobs cannot be represented"}
User: Repeat the transfer twice.
{"unsupported":"Repetition counts and missing references are unsupported"}

Output ONE JSON object with exactly ONE top-level key. NEVER repeat a JSON key.
A mixed sequential/concurrent request is one recursive instruction tree, not two
top-level instruction fields. All children of a sequence must finish in order;
children of a parallel node are independent. A sequence after a parallel group
begins only after every member of that group has finished.

Preserve EVERY reference modifier: color AND relation AND anchor identity.
Do not drop a color just because a spatial relation is also supplied. Do not pick
an ID for a descriptive reference; actual sensor grounding happens later.

User: Move parcel_10 to receiver_10 while moving parcel_11 to receiver_11; then move parcel_12 to receiver_12.
{"instruction":["sequence",["parallel",["move","parcel_10","receiver_10"],["move","parcel_11","receiver_11"]],["move","parcel_12","receiver_12"]]}
User: In parallel, perform these two branches: first move parcel_10 to receiver_10 then move parcel_11 to receiver_11; independently move parcel_12 to receiver_12.
{"instruction":["parallel",["sequence",["move","parcel_10","receiver_10"],["move","parcel_11","receiver_11"]],["move","parcel_12","receiver_12"]]}
User: Carry the green carton right of parcel_10 to receiver_11.
{"instruction":["move","green parcel right of parcel_10","receiver_11"]}
User: Where is the yellow package left of parcel_12?
{"where":"yellow parcel left of parcel_12"}
